# aither-boot-extra -- units boot starts AFTER the platform ring that are NOT in the
# kernel/platform rings of AitherOS/config/fleet_rings.yaml. Read by aither-fleet-boot-core.sh
# (/etc/aither-boot-extra first -- sync_boot_path.py installs it from origin/develop -- and this
# tracked copy as the fallback). One unit per line; `#`
# starts a comment. Before 2026-09-30 this list lived only in /etc on the host (not
# reproducible) and the GPU units the active posture declares `on` were in no boot path.
#
# GPU units stay in the `models` ring (game mode must be able to park them) and boot from here.
# check_fleet_rings.py FRG008 fails when a unit `on` in model-postures.yaml's active posture
# is not booted; FRG006 when a `requires:` dependency is not.
aither-orchestrator.service       # the brain (model-postures: on)
aither-code-embed-gguf.service    # platform embedder, 1024-d, ~1.5 GB VRAM (model-postures: on)
aither-aither-directory.service   # directory plane
aither-worker.service             # runs every routine (embed migration, backups, probes)
aither-awdiscord.service         # official Discord bot: reads the owner's DM replies (card answers + chat)
aither-cns.service                # system world model (/wm/system/*): arc.aitherium.com + universe forecasts read it
aither-world-model.service        # CPU world model: arc.aitherium.com "learning" pulse reads its /health (down after every reboot, 2026-10-23)
shadowbroker-backend.service      # shadowbroker.aitherium.com backend: HMAC agent channel + InfoNet (2026-10-28: 503 after every reboot)
shadowbroker-frontend.service     # shadowbroker.aitherium.com tunnel origin (FRG007 was blind: it read the wrong mount namespace)
aither-community-intake.service   # contribute.aitherium.com: `adk contribute upload` intake (criticality: important; 503 after reboot)
